  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aawaz II: Inclusion, Accountability and Preventing Modern Slavery - MoU</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aawaz II community engagement component has two pathways for change focusing on thematic areas of child marriage, GBV and social cohesion by i) changing awareness, attitudes and behaviors towards discrimination, intolerance, exploitation and other harmful practices ii) referrals and citizen engagement on the thematic areas and issues of exclusion and exploitation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aawaz II is an Foreign, Commonwealth &amp; Development Office (FCDO) funded programme which is being managed by British Council. Aawaz II works with local communities in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP) and Punjab provinces. The programme aims to address child marriage, gender-based violence (GBV), intolerance and community conflicts in KP and Punjab. The programme is working through community based downstream partners, developing sustainable community fora that augment and strengthen the voice of the marginalised and facilitate behaviour change.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women, youth, and other marginalised groups (transgender persons, people with disabilities (PWDs), and religious minorities).</narrative>
  </description>
